 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Ambiguities:** The standard algorithm suffers from topological ambiguities when a face has all 4 edges intersected and diagonal vertices have opposite signs (face ambiguity) or in specific internal configurations (internal ambiguity) [S5][S4, unofficial]. This can lead to holes or incorrect topology [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** If $v_1 \approx v_2$, division by zero occurs in interpolation. A small epsilon guard is required [S71, unofficial].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** The algorithm iterates up to $N-1$ for each dimension to avoid out-of-bounds access for the 8th vertex [S6, unofficial].
