 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Cubical Marching Squares Algorithm](941-cubical-marching-squares-algorithm.md)
-The Cubical Marching Squares (CMS) algorithm is an isosurface extraction method that processes voxel faces using 2D Marching Squares templates to generate line segments, which are then folded back into 3D cubes to construct a triangle mesh. It distinguishes itself from standard Marching Cubes by preserving sharp features and consistent topology without cracks.
+The Cubical Marching Squares (CMS) algorithm is an isosurface extraction method that processes voxel faces using 2D Marching Squares templates to generate line segments, which are then folded back into 3D cubes to construct a triangle mesh. It distinguishes itself from standard Marching Cubes by preserving sharp features and consistent topology without cracks. Choose it when sharp edges must be maintained without post-processing.
 
 ### [Marching Cubes 2](1393-marching-cubes-2.md)
-Marching Cubes 2 is a variant of the Marching Cubes algorithm that extracts isosurfaces from 3D scalar fields using a different lookup table or implementation strategy. It builds on the standard voxel-independent processing of Marching Cubes but modifies the core configuration logic.
